IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa17-helpers.l4: small helpers that the coa17 modules share. Layer 1, part coa17 (Part 21 and Part 21A of the
-- Companies Act 2006, ss 768 to 790ZH). Every name begins with the section label of the first provision that needs it.
--
-- SOURCE. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by
-- a converter script (inputs/SOURCES.md). It is not the official text, and nothing here is "verified against the
-- official text". The helpers quote nothing: they carry no law of their own, only the arithmetic and the three-valued
-- logic that the sections below them need.
--
-- THREE-VALUED ANSWERS (the rule of 2026-10-29). A MAYBE BOOLEAN is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING ("not covered").
-- Where a section combines two such answers, a JUST FALSE on one side settles a conjunction, a JUST TRUE on one side
-- settles a disjunction, and otherwise NOTHING stays NOTHING: a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

-- FORK NUMBERS in the comments of every coa17 module are those of NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)". The helpers carry: F1
-- (`s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` is the day plus 13, and `s 790LO(2) ...`
-- the day plus 27), F2 (month counting), F9 (an act on the last day of the period is in time).

§ `Helpers: three-valued logic`

-- s 790C(6)(a) and (b) are joined by "and"; the same helper serves every conjunction of two seam answers.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(6) both answers hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x AND y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 790C(7)(a) to (d) are alternatives; the same helper serves every disjunction of two seam answers.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790C(7) either answer holds` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x OR y)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN IF x THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Helpers: periods the text counts`

-- "within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which ..." (790D(4)(b) and every other 14-day notice):
-- the day itself is the first day of the period, so the last day is thirteen days later.
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` MEANS
    `the day the period begins` PLUS 13

-- "within the period of 28 days beginning with ..." (790LO(2), 790LP(3), 790LR(4)): the last day is 27 days later.
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790LO(2) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the day` MEANS
    `the day the period begins` PLUS 27

-- "the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which ..." (790D(3), 790G(3)): the period ends on the
-- day before the corresponding day of the next month; where the next month has no such day (a period beginning on the
-- 31st of January), it ends on the last day of that month. The Act does not state a month-counting rule (fork F2).
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day the period begins` GREATER THAN DATE_DAY (`add months` `the day the period begins` 1)
    THEN `add months` `the day the period begins` 1
    ELSE (`add months` `the day the period begins` 1) MINUS 1

-- "within two months after the date ..." (769(1), 771(1), 776(1)): the corresponding day two months later, or the last
-- day of that month where there is none (the day is not counted: the period runs after it).
GIVEN `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 769(1) the last day of the period of two months after the day` MEANS
    `add months` `the day the period runs from` 2

-- A notice or act that a section requires "within" a period that it fixes in its own words: done by the last day of the
-- period is in time; done after it is out of time (the text says no); not yet done is out of time once the period has
-- ended, and not yet decided before then. The calling section quotes its own words beside the call.
GIVEN `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day on which it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which it was done`
    WHEN JUST done THEN
        IF done AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the period that the calling section fixes in its own words (done after its last day)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the period that the calling section fixes in its own words (not done, and its last day has passed)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet done, and the period has not ended

-- "must require the person to comply with the notice by no later than the end of the period of one month beginning with
-- the day on which it is given" (790D(3), 790DA(5), 790E(3), 790EA(3)).
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the day by which the notice requires compliance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790D(3) the day required for compliance is no later than the end of the period of one month` MEANS
    IF `the day by which the notice requires compliance` AT MOST `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` `the day the notice is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by no later than the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which it is given"

§ `Helpers: penalties the text states`

-- "liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level N on the standard scale and, for continued contravention,
-- a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level N on the standard scale" (769(4), 771(4), 776(6), 790LJ(3) and
-- 790LT(3)(b)). The pounds that a level stands for are not in the Act: they are inputs where a person needs them.
GIVEN `the level on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of that level for the daily default fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 769(4) the penalty on summary conviction of a fine at a level and a daily default fine` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS `the level on the standard scale`, `fraction of the level` IS 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` WITH level IS `the level on the standard scale`, `fraction of the level` IS `the fraction of that level for the daily default fine`)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 790C(6) both answers hold` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 790C(6) both answers hold` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 790C(6) both answers hold` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 790C(6) both answers hold` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 790C(7) either answer holds` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 4 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 790D(4)(b) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day` (Date 5 1 2026) EQUALS Date 18 1 2026
